import Mathlib
import MassGap.ObsGenFam
import MassGap.LocalLink
import MassGap.ExistenceFlow

/-!
# MassGap.ObsJoint — the joint reconstruction of a family of flows, and its gap

`ObsGenFam` states clause 28 on a family of observer flows: the reconstruction space is generated by
the vectors of every member, with the two-flow Gram matrix `contSF2`. This module builds that joint
space from the lattice, for any family of flows `Φs : ℕ → Flow N` each with the uniform bound and each
keeping the positive half-space beyond one margin `r`, and proves that its time semigroup has the
Hamiltonian gap from the same lattice input as the single observer.

## The gap on the joint space (the key question)

The observer's gap is not a statement about `W`. `LocalLink.observerGap_of_runSeed` reads `RunSeed N`
as `FixedWindowDecay`, hence as `GapAt` of the gauge-invariant Wilson transfer `Dk` at every large
step at a physical rate (`ContinuumCluster.TowerGapAt`), and reads that gap on the vectors
`Yv bare k (Φ.mono k P)` through `ContinuumCluster.lattice_cluster`, which takes any two elements of
the gauge-invariant half-space algebra. The flow enters only through `UniformBoundF` (the limits
exist) and `PosPreserving τ r` (the flowed monomials lie in the half-space algebra). The two-flow
monomials `θP_n ∪ Q_m` are of the same kind, so the same argument gives, with nothing new:

* `kernJ_cluster_of_tower`: the reflected clustering bound of the joint kernel at the tower rate `μ`;
* `jointGap_of_tower`: `GapAt` of the joint transfer at every dyadic step at rate `e^{−μ a_m}`;
* `jointGap_of_runSeed`: from `RunSeed N`, one `μ > 0` with that gap for the joint transfer and for
  every member's own `flowTransfer` at every step;
* `jointOSDataS`, `jointOSDataS_hamiltonianGap`, `hamiltonianGap_joint_of_runSeed`: an `OSDataS`
  whose Hilbert space is the joint reconstruction and whose time translations are the joint
  semigroup, with `HamiltonianGap` from `RunSeed N`. The Schwinger slot `S, α, γ` of that structure
  is zero; `HamiltonianGap` does not read it.

So the gap clause on the joint space asks no gap input beyond `RunSeed N`: it is `RunSeed N` read on
more vectors of the same lattice transfer. The hypotheses the joint space adds are per member:
`UniformBoundF` of each member (for `energy0 (Wf n)`, the moments of each member) and
`PosPreserving τ r` at the one margin `r` (from a physical range at most `r`). The other clauses of
`OSDataSLinked` on the joint space (`cvec`, the links, `Reconstructs`) are not built here.

## The joint space

* `latSF2_eq_latSk`: the two-flow reading is the bare reflected reading of the flowed monomials.
* `latSk_pair_sq_le`: the reflection Cauchy–Schwarz inequality of the lattice state on the half-space
  algebra.
* `tendsto_latJ` (item 2): with each member's `UniformBoundF` and `PosPreserving τ r`, every two-flow
  reading converges along `ultra`; the bound is `|S_k(θP_n ∪ Q_m)|² ≤ S_k(θP_n ∪ P_n) S_k(θQ_m ∪ Q_m)`,
  each factor bounded by its member's own `UniformBoundF`. No normalisation beyond each member's own
  enters.
* `kernJ_symm`, `kernJ_gram_nonneg` (item 3, joint reflection positivity on `ℕ × MarginMono`),
  `kernJ_shift`, `kernJ_iterate_bound`, `kernJ_eJ`; `jointTransfer m` is `ContinuumFlow.gTransfer` of
  the joint kernel, `jointTransfer_positive`, `joint_reconstruction` (`⟪gVec p, gVec q⟫ = kernJ p q`).
* The time semigroup on the one space `HJ` (`stepJ`, `timeJ`, the port of
  `ContinuumTimeGroup`'s flowed construction to the joint kernel): `stepJ_sq`, `stepJ_eq_powT`,
  `stepJ_zero_injective`, `timeJ_dyadic`, `timeJ_add`, `timeJ_gap`, `joint_time_group`,
  `joint_generator_isSelfAdjoint`, `joint_nontrivial`.
* `jointFam`: the joint vectors `gvecJ (n, P)` meet the Gram, convergence and time clauses of
  `ObsFamily.ObsFamV` (with `X.base.time` the joint semigroup) and their closed span is the space.

## A concrete family (item 1)

`flatTail W`: `W` at `0`, the flat flow `ExistenceFlow.flatFlow (flatL N)` at every `n ≥ 1`. It is a
family of `ConfFlow N` with `flatTail W 0 = W` and `FlowRangeToZero` at every class `D`
(`flowRangeToZero_flatTail`); every member `n ≥ 1` has vanishing reach and `ClassMoments` on
`SymPlaqClass N` (`ExistenceFlow.flat_hU_hphys_hreach`). It is degenerate: `gvecJ_flat` proves that
the vectors of a member whose flowed fields are eventually constant are multiples of the vacuum, and
`span_zero_of_flat` that if every member `n ≠ 0` is such, the vectors of member `0` alone have dense
span in the joint space. The flat members' flowed fields are eventually constant
(`ObserverCarries.energy0_flat_const`). `FlowZero.flatFam` (reach ≤ `2s`, `ClassMoments` proved for
`s > 0`) is also flat. `FlowZero.apeFam` (`N = 2`) is not flat, and its moments are not proved.

## What `ObsGenFam` does not exclude

`FlowRangeToZero` bounds the members' range, not their content. `obsGen_of_famFlatTail` (proved):
at `flatTail W`, `ObsGenFamWith` gives `ObsGen` (clause 28) at `W`, generation by `W`'s vectors
included (`ObsFamily.obsGen_of_famFlat`, proved, with the flat members' vectors on the line of the
empty monomial's, `ObsFamily.v_flat_line`); on the joint space `span_zero_of_flat` (proved) puts
the space inside the closed span of member `0`'s vectors. `ObsGenFam` therefore does not by itself
force the reconstruction of the local fields; a clause that forces it needs a condition on the
members' content (for instance flowed fields that are not eventually constant at every member), not
only on their range.

Foundational footprint only (`#print axioms` after each declaration).

DERIVED (module-wide): `0` the first member, the plane, the reference step, the vanishing pairing and
the zero vector; `1` one step, the vacuum coefficient and norm, the identity; `2` the square and the
half step; `4` in `Fin 4` the spacetime dimension.
-/

noncomputable section

namespace MassGap.ObsJoint

open MassGap MassGap.InfiniteLattice MassGap.ContinuumField MassGap.ContinuumSchwinger
  MassGap.ContinuumFlow MassGap.ContinuumCluster MassGap.FlowCapstone MassGap.ContinuumTimeGroup
  MassGap.ObserverOS MassGap.ObserverOSReconstructionS MassGap.ClayFull MassGap.ObserverCarries
  MassGap.ObsFamily Filter
open scoped Topology

variable {N : ℕ}

/-! ## 1. Lattice facts -/

section Lattice

/-- **The two-flow reading is the bare reflected reading of the flowed monomials.**
DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem latSF2_eq_latSk (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φ Ψ : Flow N) (τ : Fin 4) (k : ℕ) (P Q : Mono N) :
    latSF2 hN Φ Ψ τ k P Q = latSk hN k (pairFam τ (Φ.mono k P) (Ψ.mono k Q)) := by
  have h : (Sum.elim (fun i => Φ.field k (SField.refl τ (P.2 i))) (fun j => Ψ.field k (Q.2 j))
      : Fin P.1 ⊕ Fin Q.1 → SField N) = pairFam τ (Φ.mono k P) (Ψ.mono k Q) := by
    funext x
    cases x with
    | inl i =>
      show (Φ.map k ((P.2 i).1.refl τ), (P.2 i).2.reflect τ)
        = ((Φ.map k (P.2 i).1).refl τ, (P.2 i).2.reflect τ)
      rw [Φ.map_refl]
    | inr j => rfl
  show latSk hN k (Sum.elim (fun i => Φ.field k (SField.refl τ (P.2 i)))
    (fun j => Ψ.field k (Q.2 j))) = _
  rw [h]

#print axioms latSF2_eq_latSk

/-- **Reflection Cauchy–Schwarz at step `k`**: for monomials whose products lie in the half-space
algebra, `S_k(θA ∪ B)² ≤ S_k(θA ∪ A) S_k(θB ∪ B)` (`stateK_rp` on `X + tY` at every real `t`).

DERIVED: `2` the square and the cross-term factor; `0` the plane, the sign and the discriminant. -/
theorem latSk_pair_sq_le (hN : N ≠ 0) (k : ℕ) (τ : Fin 4) (A B : Mono N)
    (hA : prodSmear (dySpacing N k) A ∈ HalfSpaceAlgebra.halfSpaceAlg (G := MassGap.SUN.SU N) τ 0)
    (hB : prodSmear (dySpacing N k) B ∈ HalfSpaceAlgebra.halfSpaceAlg (G := MassGap.SUN.SU N) τ 0) :
    latSk hN k (pairFam τ A B) ^ 2 ≤ latSk hN k (pairFam τ A A) * latSk hN k (pairFam τ B B) := by
  have ha := dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) k
  rw [latSk_eq, latSk_eq, latSk_eq, latS_pairFam _ ha, latS_pairFam _ ha, latS_pairFam _ ha]
  set X := prodSmear (dySpacing N k) A
  set Y := prodSmear (dySpacing N k) B
  have hsym := refl_pair_symm (stateK hN k) τ
    (PeriodicState.periodicState_reflInvariant hN (dyBeta (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) k) τ 0) Y X
  have hq : ∀ t : ℝ, 0 ≤ stateK hN k (LatticeReflection.ireflObs τ 0 Y * Y) * (t * t)
      + 2 * stateK hN k (LatticeReflection.ireflObs τ 0 X * Y) * t
      + stateK hN k (LatticeReflection.ireflObs τ 0 X * X) := by
    intro t
    have h0 := stateK_rp hN k τ (X + t • Y) (add_mem hA (Submodule.smul_mem _ t hB))
    have e : stateK hN k (LatticeReflection.ireflObs τ 0 (X + t • Y) * (X + t • Y))
        = stateK hN k (LatticeReflection.ireflObs τ 0 X * X)
          + t * stateK hN k (LatticeReflection.ireflObs τ 0 X * Y)
          + t * stateK hN k (LatticeReflection.ireflObs τ 0 Y * X)
          + (t * t) * stateK hN k (LatticeReflection.ireflObs τ 0 Y * Y) := by
      simp only [map_add, map_smul, add_mul, mul_add, mul_smul_comm, smul_mul_assoc,
        MassGap.DLRLimit.State.map_add, MassGap.DLRLimit.State.map_smul]
      ring
    rw [e, hsym] at h0
    nlinarith [h0]
  have hd := discrim_le_zero hq
  unfold discrim at hd
  nlinarith [hd]

#print axioms latSk_pair_sq_le

/-- **A margin monomial's flowed factors are eventually in the half-space algebra.**
DERIVED: `0` the plane. -/
theorem eventually_factor_mem (Φ : Flow N) {τ : Fin 4} {r : ℝ} (hpos : Φ.PosPreserving τ r)
    (P : MarginMono N τ r) :
    ∀ᶠ k in atTop, ∀ i : Fin P.1.1,
      smear (dySpacing N k) (Φ.map k (P.1.2 i).1).1 (P.1.2 i).2
        ∈ HalfSpaceAlgebra.halfSpaceAlg (G := MassGap.SUN.SU N) τ 0 := by
  obtain ⟨d, hd, hrd, hP⟩ := P.2
  exact Filter.eventually_all.mpr (fun i => hpos (P.1.2 i).1 (P.1.2 i).2 d hd hrd (hP i))

#print axioms eventually_factor_mem

/-- DERIVED: `0` the plane. -/
theorem eventually_mono_mem (Φ : Flow N) {τ : Fin 4} {r : ℝ} (hpos : Φ.PosPreserving τ r)
    (P : MarginMono N τ r) :
    ∀ᶠ k in atTop, prodSmear (dySpacing N k) (Φ.mono k P.1)
      ∈ HalfSpaceAlgebra.halfSpaceAlg (G := MassGap.SUN.SU N) τ 0 := by
  filter_upwards [eventually_factor_mem Φ hpos P] with k hk
  exact HalfSpaceAlgebra.halfSpaceAlg_prod_mem τ 0 Finset.univ _ (fun i _ => hk i)

#print axioms eventually_mono_mem

/-- A square bounded by `M` bounds the absolute value by `max 1 M`.
DERIVED: `1` the threshold; `2` the square. -/
theorem abs_le_max_of_sq_le {x M : ℝ} (h : x ^ 2 ≤ M) : |x| ≤ max 1 M := by
  by_cases h1 : |x| ≤ 1
  · exact le_max_of_le_left h1
  · have h1' : 1 < |x| := not_le.mp h1
    refine le_max_of_le_right (le_trans ?_ h)
    rw [← sq_abs]
    nlinarith

#print axioms abs_le_max_of_sq_le

/-- **A member's own reflected reading is eventually bounded** (`UniformBoundF` at no translation).
DERIVED: `0` the zero translation. -/
theorem eventually_abs_latSF_pair_le (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φ : Flow N) (hB : UniformBoundF hN Φ)
    (τ : Fin 4) (P : Mono N) :
    ∃ C : ℝ, ∀ᶠ k in atTop, |latSF hN Φ k (pairFam τ P P)| ≤ C := by
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := hB _ (pairFam τ P P)
  have h0 := hC 0 (fun _ => 0)
  simp only [site_zero, TestFn.translate_zero, Prod.mk.eta] at h0
  exact ⟨C, h0⟩

#print axioms eventually_abs_latSF_pair_le

/-- **A dyadic translation is a lattice translation at every finer step.**
DERIVED: `2` the dyadic ratio. -/
theorem latSk_translate_dy (hN : N ≠ 0) {k m : ℕ} (hk : m ≤ k) {ι : Type} [Fintype ι]
    (F : ι → SField N) (n : ISite) :
    latSk hN k (fun i => ((F i).1, (F i).2.translate (site (dySpacing N m) n))) = latSk hN k F := by
  rw [latSk_eq, latSk_eq, site_dySpacing N hk n]
  exact latS_translate (stateK hN k) (fun τ => PeriodicState.periodicState_shift hN _ τ)
    (dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) k) F (scaleSite (2 ^ (k - m)) n)

#print axioms latSk_translate_dy

/-- DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem mono_emptyMargin (Φ : Flow N) (k : ℕ) (τ : Fin 4) (r : ℝ) :
    Φ.mono k (emptyMargin N τ r).1 = emptyMono N :=
  mono_empty Φ k

#print axioms mono_emptyMargin

end Lattice

/-! ## 2. The joint kernel on `ℕ × MarginMono` -/

section Joint

variable (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φs : ℕ → Flow N) (τ : Fin 4) {r : ℝ}

/-- **The joint lattice reading**: `S_k(θP_n ∪ Q_m)` with `θP` flowed by member `n`, `Q` by member
`m`. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def latJ (k : ℕ) (p q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) : ℝ :=
  latSF2 hN (Φs p.1) (Φs q.1) τ k p.2.1 q.2.1

/-- **The joint kernel**: `contSF2` of the two members. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def kernJ (p q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) : ℝ :=
  contSF2 hN (Φs p.1) (Φs q.1) τ p.2.1 q.2.1

/-- **The joint step**: the dyadic shift of the monomial, the member kept. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def shJ (m : ℕ) (p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r :=
  (p.1, MarginMono.shift hN τ m p.2)

/-- **The joint vacuum**: the empty monomial of member `0`. DERIVED: `0` the first member. -/
def eJ (N : ℕ) (τ : Fin 4) (r : ℝ) : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r := (0, emptyMargin N τ r)

/-- DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem latJ_eq (k : ℕ) (p q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) :
    latJ hN Φs τ k p q
      = latSk hN k (pairFam τ ((Φs p.1).mono k p.2.1) ((Φs q.1).mono k q.2.1)) :=
  latSF2_eq_latSk hN _ _ τ k _ _

#print axioms latJ_eq

/-- DERIVED: `0` the reflection constant. -/
theorem latJ_symm (k : ℕ) (p q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) :
    latJ hN Φs τ k p q = latJ hN Φs τ k q p := by
  have ha := dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) k
  rw [latJ_eq, latJ_eq, latSk_eq, latSk_eq, latS_pairFam _ ha, latS_pairFam _ ha,
    refl_pair_symm (stateK hN k) τ
      (PeriodicState.periodicState_reflInvariant hN (dyBeta (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) k) τ 0)]

#print axioms latJ_symm

/-- **The joint kernel is symmetric.** DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem kernJ_symm (p q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) : kernJ hN Φs τ p q = kernJ hN Φs τ q p := by
  show limUnder _ (fun k => latJ hN Φs τ k p q) = limUnder _ (fun k => latJ hN Φs τ k q p)
  congr 1
  funext k
  exact latJ_symm hN Φs τ k p q

#print axioms kernJ_symm

/-- **The joint lattice Cauchy–Schwarz**, eventually in the step. DERIVED: `2` the square. -/
theorem latJ_sq_le (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r) (p q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) :
    ∀ᶠ k in atTop, latJ hN Φs τ k p q ^ 2 ≤ latJ hN Φs τ k p p * latJ hN Φs τ k q q := by
  filter_upwards [eventually_mono_mem (Φs p.1) (hpos p.1) p.2,
    eventually_mono_mem (Φs q.1) (hpos q.1) q.2] with k hp hq
  rw [latJ_eq, latJ_eq, latJ_eq]
  exact latSk_pair_sq_le hN k τ _ _ hp hq

#print axioms latJ_sq_le

/-- On the diagonal the joint reading is the member's own. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem latJ_diag (k : ℕ) (p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) :
    latJ hN Φs τ k p p = latSF hN (Φs p.1) k (pairFam τ p.2.1 p.2.1) :=
  latSF2_self hN _ τ k _ _

#print axioms latJ_diag

/-- **Item 2: every two-flow reading converges along `ultra`**, from each member's `UniformBoundF`
and `PosPreserving τ r`: `|S_k(θP_n ∪ Q_m)|² ≤ S_k(θP_n ∪ P_n) · S_k(θQ_m ∪ Q_m)`.

DERIVED: `2` the square; `1` the threshold of `abs_le_max_of_sq_le`. -/
theorem tendsto_latJ (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n)) (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r)
    (p q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) :
    Tendsto (fun k => latJ hN Φs τ k p q) (ultra : Filter ℕ) (𝓝 (kernJ hN Φs τ p q)) := by
  obtain ⟨Cp, hCp⟩ := eventually_abs_latSF_pair_le hN (Φs p.1) (hB p.1) τ p.2.1
  obtain ⟨Cq, hCq⟩ := eventually_abs_latSF_pair_le hN (Φs q.1) (hB q.1) τ q.2.1
  have hbd : ∀ᶠ k in atTop, |latJ hN Φs τ k p q| ≤ max 1 (Cp * Cq) := by
    filter_upwards [latJ_sq_le hN Φs τ hpos p q, hCp, hCq] with k hk hp hq
    refine abs_le_max_of_sq_le (hk.trans ?_)
    rw [latJ_diag, latJ_diag]
    have h1 := mul_le_mul hp hq (abs_nonneg _) ((abs_nonneg _).trans hp)
    rw [← abs_mul] at h1
    exact (le_abs_self _).trans h1
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := ContinuumSchwinger.exists_tendsto_ultra _ _ hbd
  exact tendsto_nhds_limUnder ⟨x, hx⟩

#print axioms tendsto_latJ

/-- **The joint Cauchy–Schwarz in the limit.** DERIVED: `2` the square. -/
theorem kernJ_sq_le (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n)) (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r)
    (p q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) :
    kernJ hN Φs τ p q ^ 2 ≤ kernJ hN Φs τ p p * kernJ hN Φs τ q q := by
  haveI : ((ultra : Ultrafilter ℕ) : Filter ℕ).NeBot := ultra.neBot'
  exact le_of_tendsto_of_tendsto ((tendsto_latJ hN Φs τ hB hpos p q).pow 2)
    ((tendsto_latJ hN Φs τ hB hpos p p).mul (tendsto_latJ hN Φs τ hB hpos q q))
    ((latJ_sq_le hN Φs τ hpos p q).filter_mono ultra_le)

#print axioms kernJ_sq_le

/-- **Item 3: joint reflection positivity** of `contSF2` on `ℕ × MarginMono`: at each large step the
sum is `ν_k(θX · X)` with `X = ∑ c_p ∏ smear(Φ_{p.1} …)` in the half-space algebra.

DERIVED: `0` the plane and the sign concluded. -/
theorem kernJ_gram_nonneg (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n))
    (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r) (s : Finset (ℕ × MarginMono N τ r))
    (c : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r → ℝ) :
    0 ≤ ∑ p ∈ s, ∑ q ∈ s, c p * c q * kernJ hN Φs τ p q := by
  haveI : ((ultra : Ultrafilter ℕ) : Filter ℕ).NeBot := ultra.neBot'
  have htend : Tendsto (fun k => ∑ p ∈ s, ∑ q ∈ s, c p * c q * latJ hN Φs τ k p q)
      (ultra : Filter ℕ) (𝓝 (∑ p ∈ s, ∑ q ∈ s, c p * c q * kernJ hN Φs τ p q)) :=
    tendsto_finsetSum _ (fun p _ => tendsto_finsetSum _
      (fun q _ => (tendsto_latJ hN Φs τ hB hpos p q).const_mul (c p * c q)))
  refine ge_of_tendsto htend ?_
  have hmem : ∀ᶠ k in atTop, ∀ p ∈ s, prodSmear (dySpacing N k) ((Φs p.1).mono k p.2.1)
      ∈ HalfSpaceAlgebra.halfSpaceAlg (G := MassGap.SUN.SU N) τ 0 :=
    (Filter.eventually_all_finset s).mpr (fun p _ => eventually_mono_mem (Φs p.1) (hpos p.1) p.2)
  have hev : ∀ᶠ k in atTop, 0 ≤ ∑ p ∈ s, ∑ q ∈ s, c p * c q * latJ hN Φs τ k p q := by
    filter_upwards [hmem] with k hk
    have ha := dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) k
    have hsum : ∑ p ∈ s, ∑ q ∈ s, c p * c q * latJ hN Φs τ k p q
        = ∑ p ∈ s, ∑ q ∈ s, c p * c q * stateK hN k
            (LatticeReflection.ireflObs τ 0 (prodSmear (dySpacing N k) ((Φs p.1).mono k p.2.1))
              * prodSmear (dySpacing N k) ((Φs q.1).mono k q.2.1)) := by
      refine Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun p _ => Finset.sum_congr rfl (fun q _ => ?_))
      rw [latJ_eq, latSk_eq, latS_pairFam _ ha]
    have hX : (∑ p ∈ s, c p • prodSmear (dySpacing N k) ((Φs p.1).mono k p.2.1))
        ∈ HalfSpaceAlgebra.halfSpaceAlg (G := MassGap.SUN.SU N) τ 0 :=
      Submodule.sum_mem _ (fun p hp => Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (hk p hp))
    rw [hsum]
    exact le_of_le_of_eq (stateK_rp hN k τ _ hX)
      (gram_expand (stateK hN k) (LatticeReflection.ireflObs τ 0) s c
        (fun p => prodSmear (dySpacing N k) ((Φs p.1).mono k p.2.1)))
  exact hev.filter_mono ultra_le

#print axioms kernJ_gram_nonneg

/-- DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem shJ_iterate (m n : ℕ) (p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) :
    (shJ hN τ m)^[n] p = (p.1, (MarginMono.shift hN τ m)^[n] p.2) := by
  induction n with
  | zero => rfl
  | succ n ih =>
    rw [Function.iterate_succ_apply', ih, Function.iterate_succ_apply']
    rfl

#print axioms shJ_iterate

/-- **The joint step is symmetric**: `S(θ(T P_n) ∪ Q_m) = S(θP_n ∪ T Q_m)`.
DERIVED: `1` one step and its inverse `-1`. -/
theorem kernJ_shift (m : ℕ) (p q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) :
    kernJ hN Φs τ (shJ hN τ m p) q = kernJ hN Φs τ p (shJ hN τ m q) := by
  show limUnder _ (fun k => latJ hN Φs τ k (shJ hN τ m p) q)
    = limUnder _ (fun k => latJ hN Φs τ k p (shJ hN τ m q))
  refine ContinuumSchwinger.limUnder_congr_ultra ?_
  filter_upwards [Filter.eventually_ge_atTop m] with k hk
  rw [latJ_eq, latJ_eq]
  show latSk hN k (pairFam τ (Mono.shift (timeVec N m τ 1) ((Φs p.1).mono k p.2.1))
      ((Φs q.1).mono k q.2.1))
    = latSk hN k (pairFam τ ((Φs p.1).mono k p.2.1)
      (Mono.shift (timeVec N m τ 1) ((Φs q.1).mono k q.2.1)))
  rw [ContinuumReconstruction.pairFam_shift]
  exact latSk_translate_dy hN hk _ (axisVec τ (-1))

#print axioms kernJ_shift

/-- On one member the joint kernel is the member's flowed kernel. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem kernJ_pair (n : ℕ) (P Q : MarginMono N τ r) :
    kernJ hN Φs τ (n, P) (n, Q) = kernF hN (Φs n) τ P.1 Q.1 :=
  contSF2_self hN _ τ _ _

#print axioms kernJ_pair

/-- The vacuum's member does not enter: `S(θP_n ∪ ∅) = S_n(θP ∪ ∅)`. DERIVED: `0` the first
member. -/
theorem kernJ_eJ_right (p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) :
    kernJ hN Φs τ p (eJ N τ r) = kernJ hN Φs τ p (p.1, emptyMargin N τ r) := by
  show limUnder _ (fun k => latJ hN Φs τ k p (eJ N τ r))
    = limUnder _ (fun k => latJ hN Φs τ k p (p.1, emptyMargin N τ r))
  congr 1
  funext k
  rw [latJ_eq, latJ_eq]
  show latSk hN k (pairFam τ ((Φs p.1).mono k p.2.1) ((Φs 0).mono k (emptyMargin N τ r).1))
    = latSk hN k (pairFam τ ((Φs p.1).mono k p.2.1) ((Φs p.1).mono k (emptyMargin N τ r).1))
  rw [mono_emptyMargin, mono_emptyMargin]

#print axioms kernJ_eJ_right

/-- DERIVED: `0` the first member. -/
theorem kernJ_eJ_left (q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) :
    kernJ hN Φs τ (eJ N τ r) q = kernJ hN Φs τ (q.1, emptyMargin N τ r) q := by
  rw [kernJ_symm, kernJ_eJ_right, kernJ_symm]

#print axioms kernJ_eJ_left

/-- **Iterated steps are bounded**: the diagonal is each member's own (`kernF_iterate_bound`), and
the joint Cauchy–Schwarz bounds the rest.

DERIVED: `1` the threshold of `abs_le_max_of_sq_le`. -/
theorem kernJ_iterate_bound (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n))
    (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r) (m : ℕ) (p q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) :
    ∃ C : ℝ, ∀ n : ℕ, |kernJ hN Φs τ ((shJ hN τ m)^[n] p) ((shJ hN τ m)^[n] q)| ≤ C := by
  obtain ⟨Cp, hCp⟩ := kernF_iterate_bound hN (Φs p.1) (hB p.1) τ m p.2 p.2
  obtain ⟨Cq, hCq⟩ := kernF_iterate_bound hN (Φs q.1) (hB q.1) τ m q.2 q.2
  refine ⟨max 1 (Cp * Cq), fun n => abs_le_max_of_sq_le
    ((kernJ_sq_le hN Φs τ hB hpos _ _).trans ?_)⟩
  rw [shJ_iterate, shJ_iterate, kernJ_pair, kernJ_pair]
  have h1 := mul_le_mul (hCp n) (hCq n) (abs_nonneg _) ((abs_nonneg _).trans (hCp n))
  rw [← abs_mul] at h1
  exact (le_abs_self _).trans h1

#print axioms kernJ_iterate_bound

/-- DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem shJ_eJ (m : ℕ) : shJ hN τ m (eJ N τ r) = eJ N τ r := by
  show ((0 : ℕ), MarginMono.shift hN τ m (emptyMargin N τ r)) = ((0 : ℕ), emptyMargin N τ r)
  rw [shift_emptyMargin]

#print axioms shJ_eJ

/-- DERIVED: `1` the value. -/
theorem kernJ_eJ : kernJ hN Φs τ (eJ N τ r) (eJ N τ r) = 1 :=
  contSF2_empty hN _ _ τ (r := r)

#print axioms kernJ_eJ

/-- DERIVED: `1` the half-step offset. -/
theorem shJ_half (m : ℕ) (p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) :
    shJ hN τ (m + 1) (shJ hN τ (m + 1) p) = shJ hN τ m p := by
  show (p.1, MarginMono.shift hN τ (m + 1) (MarginMono.shift hN τ (m + 1) p.2))
    = (p.1, MarginMono.shift hN τ m p.2)
  rw [MarginMono.shift_half]

#print axioms shJ_half

/-- **The joint transfer data at the dyadic step `a_m`** (`ContinuumFlow.gTransfer` of the joint
kernel). DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def jointTransfer (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n)) (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r)
    (m : ℕ) : Transfer.TransferData ((ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) →₀ ℝ) :=
  gTransfer (kernJ hN Φs τ) (kernJ_symm hN Φs τ) (kernJ_gram_nonneg hN Φs τ hB hpos)
    (shJ hN τ m) (kernJ_shift hN Φs τ m) (kernJ_iterate_bound hN Φs τ hB hpos m)
    (eJ N τ r) (shJ_eJ hN τ m) (kernJ_eJ hN Φs τ)

/-- **The joint transfer is positive** (the step `m + 1` is the half step). DERIVED: `1` the
half-step offset. -/
theorem jointTransfer_positive (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n))
    (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r) (m : ℕ) :
    GNSHilbert.PositiveTransfer (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m) := by
  unfold jointTransfer
  exact gPositive _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ (shJ hN τ (m + 1)) (kernJ_shift hN Φs τ (m + 1))
    (fun p => shJ_half hN τ m p)

#print axioms jointTransfer_positive

/-- **The joint reconstruction**: a complete Hilbert space with a unit vacuum, the transfer
self-adjoint with spectrum in `[0, 1]`, and `⟪gVec p, gVec q⟫ = kernJ p q`.

DERIVED: `0`, `1` as in `Reconstructed`. -/
theorem joint_reconstruction (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n))
    (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r) (m : ℕ) :
    Reconstructed (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m)
      ∧ ∀ p q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r,
        inner ℂ (gVec (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m) p) (gVec (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m) q)
          = (kernJ hN Φs τ p q : ℂ) :=
  ⟨reconstructed_of_positive _ (jointTransfer_positive hN Φs τ hB hpos m),
    fun p q => inner_gVec _ (kernJ hN Φs τ) (fun _ _ => rfl) p q⟩

#print axioms joint_reconstruction

end Joint

/-! ## 3. The gap of the joint transfer, from the lattice gap -/

section Gap

variable (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φs : ℕ → Flow N) (τ : Fin 4) {r : ℝ}

/-- **The joint kernel clusters at the tower rate.** If the gauge-invariant Wilson transfer has, at
every large step, `GapAt` at a rate `r'` with `μ a_k ≤ −log r'` (`TowerGapAt`), the joint kernel
obeys the reflected clustering bound at rate `μ`: `ContinuumCluster.lattice_cluster` read on the bare
monomials `(Φs n).mono k P` and `(Φs m).mono k Q`, which are elements of the gauge-invariant
half-space algebra eventually in the step.

DERIVED: `2` the square and the dyadic ratio; `0` the plane and the signs. -/
theorem kernJ_cluster_of_tower (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n))
    (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r) {μ : ℝ}
    (hT : TowerGapAt hN τ (dyBeta (one_le_of_ne_zero hN)) μ) (p q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r)
    (m n : ℕ) :
    (kernJ hN Φs τ p ((shJ hN τ m)^[n] q) - kernJ hN Φs τ p (eJ N τ r) * kernJ hN Φs τ (eJ N τ r) q)
        ^ 2
      ≤ Real.exp (-(2 * μ) * (dySpacing N m * n))
        * (kernJ hN Φs τ p p * (kernJ hN Φs τ q q - kernJ hN Φs τ (eJ N τ r) q ^ 2)) := by
  haveI : ((ultra : Ultrafilter ℕ) : Filter ℕ).NeBot := ultra.neBot'
  have hN1 := one_le_of_ne_zero hN
  have tl := tendsto_latJ hN Φs τ hB hpos
  have hf := ((tl p ((shJ hN τ m)^[n] q)).sub ((tl p (eJ N τ r)).mul (tl (eJ N τ r) q))).pow 2
  have hg := ((tl p p).mul ((tl q q).sub ((tl (eJ N τ r) q).pow 2))).const_mul
    (Real.exp (-(2 * μ) * (dySpacing N m * n)))
  refine le_of_tendsto_of_tendsto hf hg ?_
  have hT' : ∀ᶠ k in atTop, ∃ r' : ℝ, 0 < r'
      ∧ TransferGap.GapAt (DkAlong hN (dyBeta (one_le_of_ne_zero hN)) τ k) r'
      ∧ μ * dySpacing N k ≤ -Real.log r' := hT
  have hevLE : ∀ᶠ k in atTop,
      (latJ hN Φs τ k p ((shJ hN τ m)^[n] q)
          - latJ hN Φs τ k p (eJ N τ r) * latJ hN Φs τ k (eJ N τ r) q) ^ 2
        ≤ Real.exp (-(2 * μ) * (dySpacing N m * n))
          * (latJ hN Φs τ k p p * (latJ hN Φs τ k q q - latJ hN Φs τ k (eJ N τ r) q ^ 2)) := by
    filter_upwards [Filter.eventually_ge_atTop m, hT', eventually_factor_mem (Φs p.1) (hpos p.1) p.2,
      eventually_factor_mem (Φs q.1) (hpos q.1) q.2] with k hk hkr hkP hkQ
    obtain ⟨r', hr0, hg', hrate⟩ := hkr
    have hvec : site (dySpacing N k) (axisVec τ ((2 ^ (k - m) * n : ℕ) : ℤ))
        = timeVec N m τ n := by
      unfold timeVec
      rw [site_dySpacing N hk, scaleSite_axisVec]
      congr 2
    obtain ⟨hcl, hY⟩ := lattice_cluster hN (Renorm.bare N) τ (Renorm.bare_reflCompat τ) k hr0.le hg'
      ((Φs p.1).mono k p.2.1) ((Φs q.1).mono k q.2.1) (Yv_bare_mem hN τ k _ hkP)
      (Yv_bare_mem hN τ k _ hkQ) (2 ^ (k - m) * n)
    rw [hvec] at hcl
    simp only [latSkR_bare] at hcl hY
    have e1 : latJ hN Φs τ k p ((shJ hN τ m)^[n] q)
        = latSk hN k (pairFam τ ((Φs p.1).mono k p.2.1)
            ((Φs q.1).mono k (Mono.shift (timeVec N m τ n) q.2.1))) := by
      rw [latJ_eq, shJ_iterate]
      show latSk hN k (pairFam τ ((Φs p.1).mono k p.2.1)
          ((Φs q.1).mono k ((MarginMono.shift hN τ m)^[n] q.2).1)) = _
      rw [MarginMono.shift_iterate]
    have e2 : latJ hN Φs τ k p (eJ N τ r)
        = latSk hN k (pairFam τ ((Φs p.1).mono k p.2.1) (emptyMono N)) := by
      rw [latJ_eq]
      show latSk hN k (pairFam τ ((Φs p.1).mono k p.2.1) ((Φs 0).mono k (emptyMargin N τ r).1)) = _
      rw [mono_emptyMargin]
    have e3 : latJ hN Φs τ k (eJ N τ r) q
        = latSk hN k (pairFam τ (emptyMono N) ((Φs q.1).mono k q.2.1)) := by
      rw [latJ_eq]
      show latSk hN k (pairFam τ ((Φs 0).mono k (emptyMargin N τ r).1) ((Φs q.1).mono k q.2.1)) = _
      rw [mono_emptyMargin]
    rw [e1, e2, e3, latJ_eq hN Φs τ k p p, latJ_eq hN Φs τ k q q]
    have hlog : Real.log r' ≤ -μ * dySpacing N k := by linarith
    have hr_le : r' ≤ Real.exp (-μ * dySpacing N k) := by
      rw [← Real.exp_log hr0]
      exact Real.exp_le_exp.mpr hlog
    have hpow : r' ^ (2 * (2 ^ (k - m) * n)) ≤ Real.exp (-(2 * μ) * (dySpacing N m * n)) := by
      calc r' ^ (2 * (2 ^ (k - m) * n))
          ≤ Real.exp (-μ * dySpacing N k) ^ (2 * (2 ^ (k - m) * n)) :=
            pow_le_pow_left₀ hr0.le hr_le _
        _ = Real.exp (((2 * (2 ^ (k - m) * n) : ℕ) : ℝ) * (-μ * dySpacing N k)) :=
            (Real.exp_nat_mul _ _).symm
        _ = Real.exp (-(2 * μ) * (dySpacing N m * n)) := by
            rw [← dySpacing_mul_pow N hk]
            push_cast
            congr 1
            ring
    exact hcl.trans (mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_right hpow hY)
  exact hevLE.filter_mono ultra_le

#print axioms kernJ_cluster_of_tower

/-- DERIVED: `2` the square. -/
theorem exp_pow_sq (μ a : ℝ) (n : ℕ) :
    (Real.exp (-μ * a) ^ n) ^ 2 = Real.exp (-(2 * μ) * (a * n)) := by
  rw [← pow_mul, ← Real.exp_nat_mul]
  congr 1
  push_cast
  ring

#print axioms exp_pow_sq

/-- **The joint transfer is gapped at the tower rate at every dyadic step.**
DERIVED: `0` the sign of the rate. -/
theorem jointGap_of_tower (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n))
    (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r) {μ : ℝ}
    (hT : TowerGapAt hN τ (dyBeta (one_le_of_ne_zero hN)) μ) (m : ℕ) :
    TransferGap.GapAt (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m) (Real.exp (-μ * dySpacing N m)) := by
  unfold jointTransfer
  refine gapAt_gTransfer_of_cluster _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ (Real.exp_pos _).le (fun p q n => ?_)
  rw [exp_pow_sq]
  exact kernJ_cluster_of_tower hN Φs τ hB hpos hT p q m n

#print axioms jointGap_of_tower

/-- **Each member's own transfer is gapped at the same tower rate** (the joint bound restricted to
one member). DERIVED: `0` the sign of the rate. -/
theorem memberGap_of_tower (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n))
    (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r) {μ : ℝ}
    (hT : TowerGapAt hN τ (dyBeta (one_le_of_ne_zero hN)) μ) (n m : ℕ) :
    TransferGap.GapAt (flowTransfer hN (Φs n) (hB n) τ (hpos n) m)
      (Real.exp (-μ * dySpacing N m)) := by
  unfold flowTransfer
  refine gapAt_gTransfer_of_cluster _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ (Real.exp_pos _).le (fun P Q j => ?_)
  have h := kernJ_cluster_of_tower hN Φs τ hB hpos hT (n, P) (n, Q) m j
  rw [shJ_iterate, kernJ_eJ_right, kernJ_eJ_left] at h
  dsimp only at h
  rw [kernJ_pair, kernJ_pair, kernJ_pair, kernJ_pair, kernJ_pair] at h
  rw [exp_pow_sq]
  exact h

#print axioms memberGap_of_tower

/-- **The tower gap from the run seed**, at the plane `0` (`WDeltaRun.wDelta2_of_runSeed`,
`DoublingClay2.fixedWindowDecay_of_WDelta2`, `towerGapAt_dyBeta_of_fixedWindowDecay`), as in
`LocalLink.observerGap_of_runSeed`.

DERIVED: `2` the least rank; `5` the window factor; `0` the plane and the sign. -/
theorem tower_of_runSeed (hN2 : 2 ≤ N) (hfar : WDeltaRun.RunSeed N) :
    ∃ μ : ℝ, 0 < μ ∧ TowerGapAt hN 0 (dyBeta (one_le_of_ne_zero hN)) μ := by
  obtain ⟨C, hC, hW⟩ := WDeltaRun.wDelta2_of_runSeed hN hfar
  have hW' := DoublingClay2.fixedWindowDecay_of_WDelta2 hN hC (hW C (by linarith))
  obtain ⟨c, hc, hT⟩ := towerGapAt_dyBeta_of_fixedWindowDecay hN2 hN 0
    (by positivity : (0 : ℝ) < 5 * C) hW'
  exact ⟨c / (5 * C), by positivity, hT⟩

#print axioms tower_of_runSeed

/-- **The key question, answered at the transfer level.** From `RunSeed N`, one rate `μ > 0` gaps,
at every dyadic step, the joint transfer of any family with the uniform bounds and a common margin,
and every member's own flowed transfer.

DERIVED: `2` the least rank; `0` the plane and the sign. -/
theorem jointGap_of_runSeed (hN2 : 2 ≤ N) (hfar : WDeltaRun.RunSeed N)
    (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n)) (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving 0 r) :
    ∃ μ : ℝ, 0 < μ ∧ ∀ m : ℕ,
      TransferGap.GapAt (jointTransfer hN Φs 0 hB hpos m) (Real.exp (-μ * dySpacing N m))
        ∧ ∀ n : ℕ, TransferGap.GapAt (flowTransfer hN (Φs n) (hB n) 0 (hpos n) m)
          (Real.exp (-μ * dySpacing N m)) := by
  obtain ⟨μ, hμ, hT⟩ := tower_of_runSeed hN hN2 hfar
  exact ⟨μ, hμ, fun m => ⟨jointGap_of_tower hN Φs 0 hB hpos hT m,
    fun n => memberGap_of_tower hN Φs 0 hB hpos hT n m⟩⟩

#print axioms jointGap_of_runSeed

/-- **The joint transfer is `GappedAt` the tower rate** (`GapToOperator`). DERIVED: `0`, `1` the
spectral interval and the vacuum eigenvalue. -/
theorem jointGapped_of_tower (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n))
    (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r) {μ : ℝ} (hμ : 0 < μ)
    (hT : TowerGapAt hN τ (dyBeta (one_le_of_ne_zero hN)) μ) (m : ℕ) :
    ContinuumClay.GappedAt (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m) (Real.exp (-μ * dySpacing N m)) := by
  have hg := jointGap_of_tower hN Φs τ hB hpos hT m
  have hr0 : 0 < Real.exp (-μ * dySpacing N m) := Real.exp_pos _
  have hr1 : Real.exp (-μ * dySpacing N m) < 1 := by
    rw [Real.exp_lt_one_iff, neg_mul]
    exact neg_lt_zero.mpr (mul_pos hμ (dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) m))
  refine ⟨hr0, hr1, hg, fun u hu => GapToOperator.norm_opT_le_of_orth _ hr0.le hg u hu, ?_,
    GNSHilbert.isGreatest_one_spectrum_opT _⟩
  intro x hx
  rcases GapToOperator.spectrum_opT_subset _ hr0.le hg hx with h | h
  · exact Or.inl h
  · exact Or.inr ⟨Set.mem_Ici.mp
      (GNSHilbert.spectrum_opT_nonneg _ (jointTransfer_positive hN Φs τ hB hpos m) hx), h.2⟩

#print axioms jointGapped_of_tower

end Gap

/-! ## 4. The time semigroup on the joint space -/

section Time

variable (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φs : ℕ → Flow N) (τ : Fin 4) {r : ℝ}
  (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n)) (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r)

/-- **The one joint Hilbert space**: every step has the form of step `0`. DERIVED: `0` the reference
step. -/
abbrev HJ : Type := GNSHilbert.H (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm

/-- **The joint step `a_m`** on the one space. DERIVED: no numeral. -/
def stepJ (m : ℕ) : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos →L[ℂ] HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos :=
  GNSHilbert.opT (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m)

/-- **The joint vacuum.** DERIVED: `0` the reference step. -/
def vacJ : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos :=
  GNSHilbert.Omega (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).vac

/-- **The joint vector** of `(n, P)`. DERIVED: `0` the reference step. -/
def gvecJ (p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos :=
  gVec (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0) p

/-- DERIVED: `0` the reference step. -/
theorem stepJ_coe (m : ℕ) (z : GNSHilbert.Pre (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm) :
    stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m (z : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos)
      = ((GNSHilbert.Pre.ofPair (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm
          ((jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m).T (z : _ × _).1)
          ((jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m).T (z : _ × _).2)
          : GNSHilbert.Pre (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm) : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) :=
  GNSHilbert.opT_coe (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m) z

#print axioms stepJ_coe

/-- **Two half steps are one step.** DERIVED: `1` the half-step offset. -/
theorem stepJ_sq (m : ℕ) :
    stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1) * stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1) = stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m := by
  refine ContinuousLinearMap.ext (fun x => ?_)
  refine UniformSpace.Completion.induction_on x
    (isClosed_eq (stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1) * stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1)).continuous
      (stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m).continuous) (fun z => ?_)
  rw [mul_apply_eq_comp, stepJ_coe, stepJ_coe, stepJ_coe]
  congr 1
  refine GNSHilbert.Pre.ext ?_ ?_
  · show (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1)).T ((jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1)).T _)
      = (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m).T _
    exact (gT_half _ _ (fun p => shJ_half hN τ m p) _).symm
  · show (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1)).T ((jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1)).T _)
      = (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m).T _
    exact (gT_half _ _ (fun p => shJ_half hN τ m p) _).symm

#print axioms stepJ_sq

/-- DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem isSelfAdjoint_stepJ (m : ℕ) : IsSelfAdjoint (stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m) :=
  GNSHilbert.isSelfAdjoint_opT _

#print axioms isSelfAdjoint_stepJ

/-- DERIVED: `0` the order's bottom. -/
theorem stepJ_nonneg (m : ℕ) : 0 ≤ stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m :=
  (ContinuousLinearMap.nonneg_iff_isPositive _).mpr
    (GNSHilbert.isPositive_opT _ (jointTransfer_positive hN Φs τ hB hpos m))

#print axioms stepJ_nonneg

/-- DERIVED: `0`, `1` bound the spectrum. -/
theorem spectrum_stepJ (m : ℕ) : spectrum ℝ (stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m) ⊆ Set.Icc 0 1 :=
  (joint_reconstruction hN Φs τ hB hpos m).1.2.2.2.2

#print axioms spectrum_stepJ

/-- DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem stepJ_vacJ (m : ℕ) : stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m (vacJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) = vacJ hN Φs τ hB hpos :=
  GNSHilbert.opT_Omega (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m)

#print axioms stepJ_vacJ

/-- **The steps are the dyadic roots of step `0`.** DERIVED: `1/2` the dyadic ratio; `0` the
reference step. -/
theorem stepJ_eq_powT (m : ℕ) :
    stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m = powT (stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0) ((1 / 2 : ℝ) ^ m) :=
  eq_powT_of_sq (isSelfAdjoint_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0) (spectrum_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0)
    (stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) rfl (stepJ_nonneg hN Φs τ hB hpos) (stepJ_sq hN Φs τ hB hpos) m

#print axioms stepJ_eq_powT

/-- **The step moves a joint vector forward.** DERIVED: `1` the coefficient; `0` the imaginary
part. -/
theorem stepJ_gvecJ (m : ℕ) (p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) :
    stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m (gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos p) = gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (shJ hN τ m p) := by
  unfold gvecJ gVec
  rw [stepJ_coe]
  congr 1
  refine GNSHilbert.Pre.ext ?_ ?_
  · show Finsupp.mapDomain (shJ hN τ m) (Finsupp.single p 1) = Finsupp.single (shJ hN τ m p) 1
    exact Finsupp.mapDomain_single
  · show (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m).T 0 = 0
    exact map_zero _

#print axioms stepJ_gvecJ

/-- A vector killed by step `m` is killed by step `m + 1`. DERIVED: `0` the zero vector; `1` the
half-step offset. -/
theorem stepJ_succ_eq_zero {m : ℕ} {x : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos}
    (hx : stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m x = 0) : stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1) x = 0 := by
  have hsym := ContinuousLinearMap.isSelfAdjoint_iff_isSymmetric.mp
    (isSelfAdjoint_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1))
  have h1 : stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1) (stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1) x) = 0 := by
    rw [← mul_apply_eq_comp, stepJ_sq, hx]
  have h2 : inner ℂ (stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1) x) (stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1) x) = 0 := by
    have := hsym x (stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (m + 1) x)
    simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.coe_coe] at this
    rw [this, h1, inner_zero_right]
  exact inner_self_eq_zero.mp h2

#print axioms stepJ_succ_eq_zero

/-- **Orthogonal to the joint vectors is orthogonal to the pre-Hilbert space.** DERIVED: `0` the
zero combination and the imaginary part; `1` the coefficient. -/
theorem inner_pre_eq_zeroJ (x : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos)
    (horth : ∀ p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r, inner ℂ x (gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos p) = 0)
    (z : GNSHilbert.Pre (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm) :
    inner ℂ x (z : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) = 0 := by
  have hlin : ∀ c : (ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) →₀ ℝ,
      inner ℂ x ((GNSHilbert.Pre.ofPair (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm c 0
        : GNSHilbert.Pre (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm) : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos)
        = 0 := by
    intro c
    induction c using Finsupp.induction_linear with
    | zero =>
      have h0 : (GNSHilbert.Pre.ofPair (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm
          (0 : (ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) →₀ ℝ) 0
          : GNSHilbert.Pre (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm) = 0 :=
        GNSHilbert.Pre.ext rfl rfl
      rw [h0, UniformSpace.Completion.coe_zero, inner_zero_right]
    | add f g hf hg =>
      have h0 : (GNSHilbert.Pre.ofPair (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm (f + g) 0
          : GNSHilbert.Pre (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm)
          = GNSHilbert.Pre.ofPair _ f 0 + GNSHilbert.Pre.ofPair _ g 0 :=
        GNSHilbert.Pre.ext rfl
          (show (0 : (ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) →₀ ℝ) = 0 + 0 from (add_zero 0).symm)
      rw [h0, UniformSpace.Completion.coe_add, inner_add_right, hf, hg, add_zero]
    | single p b =>
      have h0 : (GNSHilbert.Pre.ofPair (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm
          (Finsupp.single p b) 0 : GNSHilbert.Pre (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm)
          = (b : ℂ) • GNSHilbert.Pre.ofPair _ (Finsupp.single p 1) 0 := by
        refine GNSHilbert.Pre.ext ?_ ?_
        · show Finsupp.single p b
            = (b : ℂ).re • Finsupp.single p (1 : ℝ)
              + (-(b : ℂ).im) • (0 : (ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) →₀ ℝ)
          simp only [Complex.ofReal_re, Complex.ofReal_im, neg_zero, zero_smul, add_zero,
            Finsupp.smul_single, smul_eq_mul, mul_one]
        · show (0 : (ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) →₀ ℝ)
            = (b : ℂ).re • (0 : (ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) →₀ ℝ) + (b : ℂ).im • Finsupp.single p (1 : ℝ)
          simp only [Complex.ofReal_im, zero_smul, smul_zero, add_zero]
      rw [h0, UniformSpace.Completion.coe_smul, inner_smul_right]
      exact mul_eq_zero_of_right _ (horth p)
  have hz : z = GNSHilbert.Pre.ofPair _ (z : _ × _).1 0
      + Complex.I • GNSHilbert.Pre.ofPair _ (z : _ × _).2 0 := by
    refine GNSHilbert.Pre.ext ?_ ?_
    · show (z : _ × _).1 = (z : _ × _).1 + (Complex.I.re • (z : _ × _).2
        + (-Complex.I.im) • (0 : (ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) →₀ ℝ))
      simp only [Complex.I_re, Complex.I_im, zero_smul, smul_zero, add_zero]
    · show (z : _ × _).2 = (0 : (ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) →₀ ℝ)
        + (Complex.I.re • (0 : (ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) →₀ ℝ) + Complex.I.im • (z : _ × _).2)
      simp only [Complex.I_re, Complex.I_im, smul_zero, one_smul, zero_add]
  rw [hz, UniformSpace.Completion.coe_add, UniformSpace.Completion.coe_smul, inner_add_right,
    inner_smul_right, hlin, hlin, mul_zero, add_zero]

#print axioms inner_pre_eq_zeroJ

/-- **Every joint vector is one step forward of a joint vector.** DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem exists_shift_preimageJ (q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r) :
    ∃ (m : ℕ) (q' : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r), shJ hN τ m q' = q := by
  obtain ⟨m, Q', hQ'⟩ := exists_shift_preimage hN τ q.2
  exact ⟨m, (q.1, Q'), by
    show (q.1, MarginMono.shift hN τ m Q') = q
    rw [hQ']⟩

#print axioms exists_shift_preimageJ

/-- **Step `0` has trivial kernel.** DERIVED: `0` the reference step and the zero vector. -/
theorem stepJ_zero_injective (x : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) (hx : stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0 x = 0) :
    x = 0 := by
  have hall : ∀ m, stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m x = 0 := by
    intro m
    induction m with
    | zero => exact hx
    | succ m ih => exact stepJ_succ_eq_zero hN Φs τ hB hpos ih
  have horth : ∀ q : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r, inner ℂ x (gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos q) = 0 := by
    intro q
    obtain ⟨m, q', hq'⟩ := exists_shift_preimageJ hN τ q
    have hsym := ContinuousLinearMap.isSelfAdjoint_iff_isSymmetric.mp
      (isSelfAdjoint_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m)
    rw [← hq', ← stepJ_gvecJ]
    have := hsym x (gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos q')
    simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.coe_coe] at this
    rw [← this, hall m, inner_zero_left]
  have hall' : ∀ y : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos, inner ℂ x y = 0 := fun y =>
    UniformSpace.Completion.induction_on y
      (isClosed_eq (continuous_const.inner continuous_id) continuous_const)
      (inner_pre_eq_zeroJ hN Φs τ hB hpos x horth)
  exact inner_self_eq_zero.mp (hall' x)

#print axioms stepJ_zero_injective

/-- **The joint time translation by `t`**: `(stepJ 0) ^ (t / a_0)`. DERIVED: `0` the reference
step. -/
def timeJ (t : ℝ) : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos →L[ℂ] HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos :=
  powT (stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0) (t / dySpacing N 0)

/-- **The time translations agree with the dyadic steps.** DERIVED: `0` the reference step; `1/2`
the dyadic ratio. -/
theorem timeJ_dyadic (m n : ℕ) :
    timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (n * dySpacing N m) = stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m ^ n := by
  have ha0 := dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) 0
  unfold timeJ
  rw [dySpacing_eq_mul N m, stepJ_eq_powT hN Φs τ hB hpos m,
    ← powT_nat_mul (isSelfAdjoint_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0) (spectrum_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0)
      (by positivity : (0 : ℝ) ≤ (1 / 2 : ℝ) ^ m) n]
  congr 1
  field_simp

#print axioms timeJ_dyadic

/-- DERIVED: `0` the time origin; `1` the identity. -/
theorem timeJ_zero : timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0 = 1 := by
  unfold timeJ
  rw [zero_div, powT_zero (isSelfAdjoint_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0)]

#print axioms timeJ_zero

/-- **The semigroup law.** DERIVED: `0` the sign of the times and the reference step. -/
theorem timeJ_add {s t : ℝ} (hs : 0 ≤ s) (ht : 0 ≤ t) :
    timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (s + t) = timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos s * timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos t := by
  have ha0 := dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) 0
  unfold timeJ
  rw [add_div, powT_add (spectrum_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0) (div_nonneg hs ha0.le)
    (div_nonneg ht ha0.le)]

#print axioms timeJ_add

/-- **Positive self-adjoint contractions.** DERIVED: `0` the order's bottom and the sign of `t`;
`1` the norm bound. -/
theorem timeJ_nonneg_norm (t : ℝ) (ht : 0 ≤ t) :
    0 ≤ timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos t ∧ IsSelfAdjoint (timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos t)
      ∧ ‖timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos t‖ ≤ 1 :=
  ⟨powT_nonneg (spectrum_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0) _, isSelfAdjoint_powT _,
    norm_powT_le_one (spectrum_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0)
      (div_nonneg ht (dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) 0).le)⟩

#print axioms timeJ_nonneg_norm

/-- **Strong continuity on `[0, ∞)`.** DERIVED: `0` the time origin and the reference step. -/
theorem continuousOn_timeJ (y : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) :
    ContinuousOn (fun t => timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos t y) (Set.Ici 0) := by
  have ha0 := dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) 0
  have hc := continuousOn_powT_apply (isSelfAdjoint_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0)
    (spectrum_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0) (stepJ_zero_injective hN Φs τ hB hpos) y
  have hd : ContinuousOn (fun t : ℝ => t / dySpacing N 0) (Set.Ici 0) :=
    (continuous_id.div_const _).continuousOn
  exact hc.comp hd (fun t ht => div_nonneg ht ha0.le)

#print axioms continuousOn_timeJ

/-- **The vacuum is invariant.** DERIVED: `0` the sign of `t` and the reference step; `1/2` the
dyadic ratio. -/
theorem timeJ_vacJ {t : ℝ} (ht : 0 ≤ t) :
    timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos t (vacJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) = vacJ hN Φs τ hB hpos := by
  have ha0 := dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) 0
  refine powT_apply_fixed (isSelfAdjoint_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0)
    (spectrum_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0) (fun m n => ?_) (div_nonneg ht ha0.le)
  rw [powT_nat_mul (isSelfAdjoint_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0) (spectrum_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0)
    (by positivity) n, ← stepJ_eq_powT]
  induction n with
  | zero => rw [pow_zero, one_apply_eq_self]
  | succ n ih => rw [pow_succ, mul_apply_eq_comp, stepJ_vacJ, ih]

#print axioms timeJ_vacJ

/-- **The dyadic gaps give the gap at every time** on the joint space. DERIVED: `0` the sign of `μ`
and `t`, the vanishing pairing and the reference step; `1` the vacuum eigenvalue; `1/2` the dyadic
ratio. -/
theorem timeJ_gap {μ : ℝ} (hμ : 0 ≤ μ)
    (hgap : ∀ m : ℕ, ContinuumClay.GappedAt (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos m)
      (Real.exp (-μ * dySpacing N m))) {t : ℝ} (ht : 0 ≤ t) :
    (∀ u : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos, inner ℂ (vacJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) u = 0 →
        ‖timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos t u‖ ≤ Real.exp (-(μ * t)) * ‖u‖)
      ∧ spectrum ℝ (timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos t) ⊆ {1} ∪ Set.Icc 0 (Real.exp (-(μ * t))) := by
  have ha0 := dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) 0
  have hsa := isSelfAdjoint_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0
  have hsp := spectrum_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0
  have htime : μ * dySpacing N 0 * (t / dySpacing N 0) = μ * t := by field_simp
  refine ⟨fun u hu => ?_, ?_⟩
  · have hd : ∀ m n : ℕ, ‖powT (stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0) (n * (1 / 2 : ℝ) ^ m) u‖
        ≤ Real.exp (-(μ * dySpacing N 0 * (n * (1 / 2 : ℝ) ^ m))) * ‖u‖ := by
      intro m n
      rw [powT_nat_mul hsa hsp (by positivity) n, ← stepJ_eq_powT]
      have hsym := ContinuousLinearMap.isSelfAdjoint_iff_isSymmetric.mp
        (isSelfAdjoint_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m)
      have hstep : ∀ v : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos, inner ℂ (vacJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) v = 0 →
          ‖stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m v‖ ≤ Real.exp (-μ * dySpacing N m) * ‖v‖ :=
        fun v hv => (hgap m).2.2.2.1 v hv
      have hinv : ∀ v : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos, inner ℂ (vacJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) v = 0 →
          inner ℂ (vacJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) (stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m v) = 0 := by
        intro v hv
        have := hsym (vacJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) v
        simp only [ContinuousLinearMap.coe_coe] at this
        rw [← this, stepJ_vacJ, hv]
      have hpow : ∀ k : ℕ,
          inner ℂ (vacJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) ((stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m ^ k) u) = 0
          ∧ ‖(stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m ^ k) u‖ ≤ Real.exp (-μ * dySpacing N m) ^ k * ‖u‖ := by
        intro k
        induction k with
        | zero =>
          rw [pow_zero, one_apply_eq_self, pow_zero, one_mul]
          exact ⟨hu, le_rfl⟩
        | succ k ih =>
          rw [pow_succ', mul_apply_eq_comp]
          refine ⟨hinv _ ih.1, (hstep _ ih.1).trans ?_⟩
          rw [pow_succ', mul_assoc]
          exact mul_le_mul_of_nonneg_left ih.2 (Real.exp_pos _).le
      refine (hpow n).2.trans (le_of_eq ?_)
      rw [← Real.exp_nat_mul, dySpacing_eq_mul N m]
      congr 2
      ring
    have h := norm_powT_apply_le hsa hsp (mul_nonneg hμ ha0.le) hd (div_nonneg ht ha0.le)
    rw [htime] at h
    exact h
  · have hgap0 : spectrum ℝ (stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0)
        ⊆ {1} ∪ Set.Icc 0 (Real.exp (-μ * dySpacing N 0)) := (hgap 0).2.2.2.2.1
    have h := spectrum_powT_subset hsa hsp hgap0 (div_nonneg ht ha0.le)
    rw [← Real.exp_mul] at h
    have e : -μ * dySpacing N 0 * (t / dySpacing N 0) = -(μ * t) := by field_simp
    rw [e] at h
    exact h

#print axioms timeJ_gap

/-- **The generator of the joint time semigroup is self-adjoint.** DERIVED: `0` the reference
step. -/
theorem joint_generator_isSelfAdjoint :
    IsSelfAdjoint (ClassHamiltonian.generator (timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos)) :=
  ClassHamiltonian.powSemigroup_generator_isSelfAdjoint (isSelfAdjoint_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0)
    (spectrum_stepJ hN Φs τ hB hpos 0) (stepJ_zero_injective hN Φs τ hB hpos)
    (dySpacing_pos (one_le_of_ne_zero hN) 0)

#print axioms joint_generator_isSelfAdjoint

/-- **A non-zero vector orthogonal to the joint vacuum**, from `FlowConnectedNonzero` of one member.
DERIVED: `0` the vanishing pairing, the zero vector and the reference step; `1` the coefficient;
`2` the square. -/
theorem joint_nontrivial (n0 : ℕ) (hNT : FlowConnectedNonzero hN (Φs n0) τ r) :
    ∃ u : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos, inner ℂ (vacJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) u = 0 ∧ u ≠ 0 := by
  obtain ⟨Q, hQ⟩ := hNT
  have hx : (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).form (Finsupp.single (n0, Q) 1)
        (Finsupp.single (n0, Q) 1)
      - (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).form (Finsupp.single (n0, Q) 1)
          (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).vac ^ 2 ≠ 0 := by
    show gForm (kernJ hN Φs τ) (Finsupp.single (n0, Q) 1) (Finsupp.single (n0, Q) 1)
      - gForm (kernJ hN Φs τ) (Finsupp.single (n0, Q) 1) (Finsupp.single (eJ N τ r) 1) ^ 2 ≠ 0
    rw [gForm_single, gForm_single]
    simp only [one_mul]
    rw [kernJ_eJ_right]
    dsimp only
    rw [kernJ_pair, kernJ_pair, ← kernF_symm hN (Φs n0) τ (emptyMargin N τ r).1 Q.1]
    exact hQ
  exact ContinuumSep.exists_orth_ne_zero (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0) _ hx

#print axioms joint_nontrivial

/-- **The continuous-time picture on the joint space at the tower rate.** -/
theorem joint_time_group {μ : ℝ} (hμ : 0 < μ)
    (hT : TowerGapAt hN τ (dyBeta (one_le_of_ne_zero hN)) μ) {t : ℝ} (ht : 0 ≤ t) :
    (∀ u : HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos, inner ℂ (vacJ hN Φs τ hB hpos) u = 0 →
        ‖timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos t u‖ ≤ Real.exp (-(μ * t)) * ‖u‖)
      ∧ spectrum ℝ (timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos t) ⊆ {1} ∪ Set.Icc 0 (Real.exp (-(μ * t))) :=
  timeJ_gap hN Φs τ hB hpos hμ.le (jointGapped_of_tower hN Φs τ hB hpos hμ hT) ht

#print axioms joint_time_group

end Time

/-! ## 5. The Hamiltonian gap on the joint space -/

section Hamiltonian

variable (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φs : ℕ → Flow N) (τ : Fin 4) {r : ℝ}
  (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n)) (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r)

/-- **The joint reconstruction as `OSDataS`**: the Hilbert space `HJ`, the vacuum `vacJ`, the time
translations `timeJ`, the gap the tower rate `μ`. The Schwinger slot is zero. It is not the joint
Schwinger functions, and `HamiltonianGap` does not read it.

DERIVED: `0` the Schwinger slot and its constants, the sign of `μ` and `t`. -/
def jointOSDataS {μ : ℝ} (hμ : 0 < μ)
    (hT : TowerGapAt hN τ (dyBeta (one_le_of_ne_zero hN)) μ) (n0 : ℕ)
    (hNT : FlowConnectedNonzero hN (Φs n0) τ r) : OSDataS where
  S := fun _ => 0
  α := 0
  γ := 0
  growth := fun n φ => by simp
  os3 := fun n σ φ => rfl
  H := HJ hN Φs τ hB hpos
  vac := vacJ hN Φs τ hB hpos
  time := timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos
  gap := μ
  gap_pos := hμ
  time_zero := timeJ_zero hN Φs τ hB hpos
  time_add := fun _ _ hs ht => timeJ_add hN Φs τ hB hpos hs ht
  time_selfAdjoint := fun t ht =>
    ⟨(timeJ_nonneg_norm hN Φs τ hB hpos t ht).2.1, (timeJ_nonneg_norm hN Φs τ hB hpos t ht).2.2⟩
  time_cont := continuousOn_timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos
  time_vac := fun _ ht => timeJ_vacJ hN Φs τ hB hpos ht
  time_gap := fun _ ht => (joint_time_group hN Φs τ hB hpos hμ hT ht).1
  nontrivial := joint_nontrivial hN Φs τ hB hpos n0 hNT

/-- **`HamiltonianGap` on the joint space.** DERIVED: no numeral. -/
theorem jointOSDataS_hamiltonianGap {μ : ℝ} (hμ : 0 < μ)
    (hT : TowerGapAt hN τ (dyBeta (one_le_of_ne_zero hN)) μ) (n0 : ℕ)
    (hNT : FlowConnectedNonzero hN (Φs n0) τ r) :
    HamiltonianGap (jointOSDataS hN Φs τ hB hpos hμ hT n0 hNT) :=
  hamiltonianGap_of_selfAdjoint _ (joint_generator_isSelfAdjoint hN Φs τ hB hpos)

#print axioms jointOSDataS_hamiltonianGap

/-- **The key question: the joint space has the Hamiltonian gap from `RunSeed N`**, at the plane `0`,
for every family with each member's `UniformBoundF`, a common margin, and one member with
`FlowConnectedNonzero`. No gap input beyond `RunSeed N` enters.

DERIVED: `2` the least rank; `0` the plane and the sign. -/
theorem hamiltonianGap_joint_of_runSeed (hN2 : 2 ≤ N) (hfar : WDeltaRun.RunSeed N)
    (Φs : ℕ → Flow N) (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n))
    (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving 0 r) (n0 : ℕ)
    (hNT : FlowConnectedNonzero hN (Φs n0) 0 r) :
    ∃ (μ : ℝ) (hμ : 0 < μ) (hT : TowerGapAt hN 0 (dyBeta (one_le_of_ne_zero hN)) μ),
      HamiltonianGap (jointOSDataS hN Φs 0 hB hpos hμ hT n0 hNT) := by
  obtain ⟨μ, hμ, hT⟩ := tower_of_runSeed hN hN2 hfar
  exact ⟨μ, hμ, hT, jointOSDataS_hamiltonianGap hN Φs 0 hB hpos hμ hT n0 hNT⟩

#print axioms hamiltonianGap_joint_of_runSeed

/-- **The joint vectors meet the clauses of `ObsFamV` other than `v 0 = X.cvec`**, with the joint
semigroup as the time: convergence of every two-flow reading with `⟪v n P, v m Q⟫ = contSF2`, the
time step `a_m` acting as the dyadic shift on every member, and closed span the whole space.

DERIVED: `1` one step. -/
theorem jointFam :
    (∀ (n m : ℕ) (P Q : MarginMono N τ r),
      Tendsto (fun k => latSF2 hN (Φs n) (Φs m) τ k P.1 Q.1) (ultra : Filter ℕ)
          (𝓝 (contSF2 hN (Φs n) (Φs m) τ P.1 Q.1))
        ∧ inner ℂ (gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (n, P)) (gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (m, Q))
          = (contSF2 hN (Φs n) (Φs m) τ P.1 Q.1 : ℂ))
    ∧ (∀ (n m : ℕ) (P Q : MarginMono N τ r),
      Q.1 = ⟨P.1.1, fun i => ((P.1.2 i).1, (P.1.2 i).2.translate (timeVec N m τ 1))⟩ →
        gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (n, Q)
          = timeJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (dySpacing N m) (gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (n, P)))
    ∧ (Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range (gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos))).topologicalClosure = ⊤ := by
  refine ⟨fun n m P Q => ⟨tendsto_latJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (n, P) (m, Q),
    (joint_reconstruction hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).2 (n, P) (m, Q)⟩, fun n m P Q hQ => ?_,
    ClayStatement.span_single_dense (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm⟩
  have e : Q = MarginMono.shift hN τ m P := Subtype.ext hQ
  have ht := timeJ_dyadic hN Φs τ hB hpos m 1
  rw [Nat.cast_one, one_mul, pow_one] at ht
  rw [e, ht]
  exact (stepJ_gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos m (n, P)).symm

#print axioms jointFam

end Hamiltonian

/-! ## 6. A concrete family, and the degenerate members -/

section FlatTail

/-- **`W` followed by the flat flow**: `W` at `0`, `flatFlow (flatL N)` at every `n ≥ 1`.
DERIVED: `0` the first member; `1` the successor. -/
def flatTail (W : ConfFlow N) : ℕ → ConfFlow N
  | 0 => W
  | _ + 1 => ExistenceFlow.flatFlow (N := N) (ExistenceFlow.flatL N)

/-- DERIVED: `0` the first member. -/
theorem flatTail_zero (W : ConfFlow N) : flatTail W 0 = W := rfl

#print axioms flatTail_zero

/-- **The flat tail meets `FlowRangeToZero` at every class** (`ExistenceFlow.flat_reach`).
DERIVED: `1` the first flat member; `0` the limit. -/
theorem flowRangeToZero_flatTail (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N)
    (D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)))
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D) :
    FlowRangeToZero D hD (flatTail W) := by
  intro r' hr'
  rw [Filter.eventually_atTop]
  refine ⟨1, fun n hn => ?_⟩
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ : ∃ m, n = m + 1 := ⟨n - 1, by omega⟩
  exact (ExistenceFlow.flat_reach hN).eventually (eventually_le_nhds hr')

#print axioms flowRangeToZero_flatTail

/-- **At `flatTail W`, `ObsGenFamWith` gives `ObsGen` (clause 28) at `W`**: the members `n ≥ 1` are
flat (`ObserverCarries.energy0_flat_const`), so `ObsFamily.obsGen_of_famFlat` applies.

DERIVED: `1` the successor. -/
theorem obsGen_of_famFlatTail (hN : N ≠ 0) (W : ConfFlow N)
    {D : Set (LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N))} {τ : Fin 4} {r : ℝ}
    (hD : ∀ (τ : Fin 4) (O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N)), O.refl τ ∈ D ↔ O ∈ D)
    (X : ObserverOSLinked.OSDataSLinked N D τ r) (h : ObsGenFamWith hN W D hD X (flatTail W)) :
    ClayStatement.ObsGen hN W D hD X :=
  obsGen_of_famFlat hN W hD X _ h (fun n hn O => by
    obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ : ∃ m, n = m + 1 := ⟨n - 1, by omega⟩
    exact energy0_flat_const (ExistenceFlow.tendsto_flatL hN) D hD O)

#print axioms obsGen_of_famFlatTail

end FlatTail

section Flat

variable (hN : N ≠ 0) (Φs : ℕ → Flow N) (τ : Fin 4) {r : ℝ}
  (hB : ∀ n, UniformBoundF hN (Φs n)) (hpos : ∀ n, (Φs n).PosPreserving τ r)

/-- **A member with eventually constant flowed fields has its vectors on the vacuum line**:
`gvecJ (n, P) = S(θP_n ∪ ∅) · Ω`, since `S(θP_n ∪ P_n) = S(θP_n ∪ ∅)²` (`latSF2_factor`).

DERIVED: `0` the zero vector; `1` the vacuum norm; `2` the square. -/
theorem gvecJ_flat (n : ℕ) (hC : ∀ O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N), ∀ᶠ k in atTop, CstAt (Φs n) k O)
    (P : MarginMono N τ r) :
    gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (n, P)
      = (kernJ hN Φs τ (n, P) (eJ N τ r) : ℂ) • gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos (eJ N τ r) := by
  haveI : ((ultra : Ultrafilter ℕ) : Filter ℕ).NeBot := ultra.neBot'
  set p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r := (n, P)
  set e := eJ N τ r
  have hev : ∀ᶠ k in atTop, latJ hN Φs τ k p p = latJ hN Φs τ k p e * latJ hN Φs τ k e p := by
    filter_upwards [Filter.eventually_all.2 (fun i => hC (SField.refl τ (P.1.2 i)).1),
      Filter.eventually_all.2 (fun j => hC (P.1.2 j).1)] with k hP hQ
    exact latSF2_factor hN (Φs n) (Φs n) (Φs 0) (Φs 0) τ (r := r) k P.1 P.1 hP hQ
  have hpp : kernJ hN Φs τ p p = kernJ hN Φs τ p e * kernJ hN Φs τ e p :=
    tendsto_nhds_unique (tendsto_latJ hN Φs τ hB hpos p p)
      (((tendsto_latJ hN Φs τ hB hpos p e).mul (tendsto_latJ hN Φs τ hB hpos e p)).congr'
        (EventuallyEq.symm (hev.filter_mono ultra_le)))
  have hin := (joint_reconstruction hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).2
  set c : ℝ := kernJ hN Φs τ p e
  have hep : kernJ hN Φs τ e p = c := kernJ_symm hN Φs τ e p
  have hee : kernJ hN Φs τ e e = 1 := kernJ_eJ hN Φs τ
  have hd : inner ℂ (gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos p - (c : ℂ) • gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos e)
      (gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos p - (c : ℂ) • gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos e) = 0 := by
    simp only [inner_sub_left, inner_sub_right, inner_smul_left, inner_smul_right]
    have h1 := hin p p
    have h2 := hin p e
    have h3 := hin e p
    have h4 := hin e e
    unfold gvecJ
    rw [h1, h2, h3, h4, hpp, hep, hee, Complex.conj_ofReal]
    push_cast
    ring
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp (inner_self_eq_zero.mp hd)

#print axioms gvecJ_flat

/-- **If every member `n ≠ 0` has eventually constant flowed fields, the vectors of member `0` alone
have dense span in the joint space.**

DERIVED: `0` the first member. -/
theorem span_zero_of_flat
    (hC : ∀ n : ℕ, n ≠ 0 → ∀ O : LField (MassGap.SUN.SU N), ∀ᶠ k in atTop, CstAt (Φs n) k O) :
    (Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range (fun P : MarginMono N τ r =>
      gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos ((0 : ℕ), P)))).topologicalClosure = ⊤ := by
  set S := Submodule.span ℂ (Set.range (fun P : MarginMono N τ r =>
      gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos ((0 : ℕ), P)))
  have hmem : ∀ p : ℕ × MarginMono N τ r, gvecJ hN Φs τ hB hpos p ∈ S := by
    rintro ⟨n, P⟩
    by_cases hn : n = 0
    · subst hn
      exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨P, rfl⟩
    · rw [gvecJ_flat hN Φs τ hB hpos n (hC n hn) P]
      exact S.smul_mem _ (Submodule.subset_span ⟨emptyMargin N τ r, rfl⟩)
  refine top_le_iff.mp ?_
  rw [← ClayStatement.span_single_dense (jointTransfer hN Φs τ hB hpos 0).toReflForm]
  refine Submodule.topologicalClosure_mono (Submodule.span_le.mpr ?_)
  rintro _ ⟨p, rfl⟩
  exact hmem p

#print axioms span_zero_of_flat

end Flat

